From 2329fdee5b21f69ec82f5bbfb8eea2e0a99e1305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:29:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: small savings on the main thread's path: cold code
 apart, returns take the PC from registers, plain TLS reads

- dynarmic A32 (UserConfig::split_cold_code, on in Eden): a block's deferred emits go to cold
  chunks taken from the code cache's top down while blocks fill it upwards (bounded up front,
  the chunk's end the assembler's limit while written; inline as before if too large).
- An inline return or fast dispatch whose block ends with BXWritePC takes the new PC and upper
  location descriptor from ecx/ebx instead of loading back what it just stored.
- KernelCore's thread-local data trivially destructible (constinit; the dummy KThread a thread
  may own a thread-local of its own): GetCurrentEmuThread without __tls_init.
- CoreTiming::UnscheduleEvent compares owners instead of lock()ing each queued weak pointer.
- The services' host threads spin up to 250 us (twice their last wait) after a short wait,
  50 us otherwise; their wakes are counted for the launcher's log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
